1
00:01:48,276 --> 00:01:51,876
أعوذ بالله من الشيطان الرجيم ۞بِسمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحمٰنِ الرَّحيمِ۞

2
00:01:51,979 --> 00:01:57,442
اَلْحَمْدُ لله  وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِالْاَوَّلِيْنَ وَالْآخِرِيْنَ محمد اِبْنِ عَبْدُ الله

3
00:01:57,586 --> 00:02:00,886
وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْراً اَمَّابَعْدَ

4
00:02:01,647 --> 00:02:04,521
اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَةُ الله وَبَرَكَاتُهُ

5
00:02:06,406 --> 00:02:11,877
يَقُوْلُ تَعَالَى: يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا اتَّقُوا اللَّهَ حَقَّ تُقَاتِهِ وَلَا تَمُوتُنَّ إِلَّا وَأَنْتُمْ مُسْلِمُونَ۞

6
00:02:12,363 --> 00:02:13,356
Allahعَزّ وجَلّ says:

7
00:02:13,396 --> 00:02:18,227
O you, who believe do not let death approach you, except in state of Taqwa(تَقوى).

8
00:02:18,248 --> 00:02:20,472
We ask Allahعَزّ وجَلّ to give us all, Taqwa(تقوى).

9
00:02:21,807 --> 00:02:28,056
In Sunan Al-Baghawi(سُنَنْ اَلْبَغْوِيْ), Abdullah Ibn Masood رضي الله عنه says;

10
00:02:28,640 --> 00:02:35,945
مَنْ كَانَ مُسْتَنًّا فَلْيَسْتَنَّ بِمَنْ قَدْ مَاتْ، فَإنَّ الْحَيَّ لَا تُؤمَنُ عَلَيْهِ الْفِتْنَةَ

11
00:02:36,532 --> 00:02:42,407
أوْلَئكَ أصْحَابُ محمد، صَلَوَاتُ الله وَسَلَامُ عَلَيْهَ

12
00:02:44,307 --> 00:02:46,357
كَانُوْا وَالله أفْضَلَ هَذِهِ الّأمَّةَ

13
00:02:46,761 --> 00:02:52,043
وَأبَرُّهَا قُلُوْبًا ، وَأعْمَقُهَا عِلْمًا، وَأقَلُهَا تَكَلُفًا

14
00:02:52,760 --> 00:02:56,359
قَوْمُ اُخْتَارَهُمُ الله لِصَحْبَةِ نَبِيِّهِ وَإقَامَةِ دِيْنِه

15
00:02:57,590 --> 00:03:01,619
فَإعْرَفُوْا لَهُمْ فَضْلَهُمْ ، وَأتْبَعُوْ هُمْ فِيْ أثَارِهِمْ

16
00:03:02,107 --> 00:03:07,518
وَتَمَسَّكُوْا بِمَا أسْتَطَعْتُمْ مِنْ أخْلَاقِهِمْ وَ دِيْنِهِمْ ، فَإنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا عَلَى الصَّرَاطِ الّمُسْتَقٍيْمَ

17
00:03:09,523 --> 00:03:11,791
Abdullah Ibn Masood رضي الله عنه says;

18
00:03:11,821 --> 00:03:15,074
مَنْ كَانَ مُسْتَنًّا فَلْيَسْتَنَّ بِمَنْ قَدْ مَاتْ

19
00:03:16,386 --> 00:03:21,946
Whoever, is gonna follow a path, should follow the path of the ones, who died,

20
00:03:23,467 --> 00:03:25,620
فَإنَّ الْحَيَّ لَا تُؤمَنُ عَلَيْهِ الْفِتْنَةََ

21
00:03:26,186 --> 00:03:28,953
Because the living could fail in their trials,

22
00:03:30,432 --> 00:03:32,294
أوْلَئكَ أصْحَابُ محمد

23
00:03:33,199 --> 00:03:37,115
Those are the companions of Muhammadﷺ,

24
00:03:37,965 --> 00:03:41,577
Abdullah Ibn Masood رضي الله عنه is telling the Taba'een(تَا بَعِيْن),

25
00:03:42,867 --> 00:03:46,001
who are the second greatest generation, he is telling them:

26
00:03:47,998 --> 00:03:50,266
Don’t follow the living among you,

27
00:03:51,515 --> 00:03:54,168
even though some of these might be Aouleaa(أؤلِيآء) of Allahعَزّ وجَلّ

28
00:03:54,193 --> 00:03:57,923
some of them might be Virtuous, Mujahideen(مجاهدين), Ulema(علماء), Ubbaad(عُبَّاد).

29
00:03:58,904 --> 00:04:00,597
Abdullah Ibn Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود), is telling them:

30
00:04:00,651 --> 00:04:03,341
Don’t follow the living among you, but follow the dead,

31
00:04:03,471 --> 00:04:05,753
the companions of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

32
00:04:06,211 --> 00:04:06,727
Why?

33
00:04:07,118 --> 00:04:11,826
Because there is no guarantee, this person, who is living, wouldn’t fail in some of his trials.

34
00:04:14,459 --> 00:04:18,284
But with Sahabahرضي الله عنهم, they have been given the stamp of approval.

35
00:04:19,822 --> 00:04:23,199
See, with anyone, who is living, you never know, what the outcome would be?

36
00:04:23,928 --> 00:04:25,368
Because Rasool Allah ﷺ says:

37
00:04:25,388 --> 00:04:32,827
There are some people, who would be on the track of people of Jannah(جنة), in their Ibadah(عبادة), in their action.

38
00:04:33,014 --> 00:04:35,034
They are doing what people of Jannah(جنة) do,

39
00:04:35,941 --> 00:04:41,714
but before they die, they commit the actions of people of Hell Fire and then they end up going to Hell fire.

40
00:04:43,080 --> 00:04:46,118
Why? They failed in Fitnah(فِتْنَه), Trials.

41
00:04:46,741 --> 00:04:48,878
Everyone is going be faced with the trials

42
00:04:49,183 --> 00:04:51,669
and nobody knows what the outcome of that will be?

43
00:04:52,768 --> 00:04:54,371
And that is why Rasool Allah ﷺ used to say:

44
00:04:54,396 --> 00:04:57,792
"يَا مُقَلِّبَ الْقُلُوْبِ وَالْاَبْصَارْ ثَبِّتْ قُلُوْبَنَا عَلَى الدِيْنِكْ"

45
00:04:58,426 --> 00:05:02,392
O the One, Who changes the hearts, make our hearts steadfast on Islam.

46
00:05:03,089 --> 00:05:05,994
The heart, the word Qalb(قلب), in Arabic means "something that changes",

47
00:05:06,019 --> 00:05:08,109
overturns, goes up and down.

48
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:13,564
So, Abdullah Ibn Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود) is saying: Follow the companions of Rasool Ullah.

49
00:05:14,348 --> 00:05:18,674
He was saying this, in time of Taba'een(تَابَعِيْن), which were the second best generation.

50
00:05:18,699 --> 00:05:21,051
What should, we say today?

51
00:05:22,835 --> 00:05:26,942
No one has the guarantee, no one, that they are going to go to Jannah(جنة). Nobody!

52
00:05:28,860 --> 00:05:33,895
But the ones, who were with Rasool Allah ﷺ, the ones, who were in Ghazwat Al-Badr(غزوة البدر),

53
00:05:34,491 --> 00:05:37,028
the ones, who gave him Bay'ah(بيعة) under, Ar-Ridwan(الرضوان),

54
00:05:37,818 --> 00:05:40,809
the ones, who fought with him, the one, who had patience with him,

55
00:05:41,094 --> 00:05:43,350
the ones whom, when Rasool Allah ﷺ died,

56
00:05:43,877 --> 00:05:45,354
مَاتَّ وَّهُوَعَنْهُمْ رَاضِي

57
00:05:46,391 --> 00:05:49,748
Rasool Allah ﷺ was pleased with them, these are the ones, we should follow.

58
00:05:50,681 --> 00:05:53,864
And then he gives us some other reasons, why should, we should follow them.? He says;

59
00:05:54,555 --> 00:05:56,168
كَانُوْا وَالله أفْضَلَ هَذِهِ الّأمَّةَ

60
00:05:56,193 --> 00:05:57,378
They were the best of this Ummah(امة).

61
00:05:59,615 --> 00:06:01,354
خَيْرُالْقُرُوْنِيْ قَرْنِيْ

62
00:06:02,150 --> 00:06:05,775
Rasool Allah ﷺ says: The best of generations, is my generation.

63
00:06:06,304 --> 00:06:07,324
These are the best!

64
00:06:09,240 --> 00:06:13,909
كَانُوْا وَالله أفْضَلَ هَذِهِ الّأمَّةَ وَأبَرُّهَا قُلُوْبًا

65
00:06:14,686 --> 00:06:16,731
And they had the most pious hearts.

66
00:06:17,708 --> 00:06:19,405
Their hearts had the most Taqwa(تَقْوى).

67
00:06:19,970 --> 00:06:22,994
No one can compete with the Sahabah(صحابه) in their Taqwa(تَقْوى).

68
00:06:24,841 --> 00:06:26,647
They've achieved the highest limits.

69
00:06:28,865 --> 00:06:30,528
وَأعْمَقُهَا عِلْمًا

70
00:06:32,087 --> 00:06:34,103
And they had the deepest knowledge.

71
00:06:34,287 --> 00:06:36,354
Now, notice here the choice of words.

72
00:06:37,105 --> 00:06:38,369
Abdullah Ibn Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود) didn’t say,

73
00:06:38,394 --> 00:06:39,774
"وَاَكْثَرُهَا عِلْمًا"

74
00:06:40,379 --> 00:06:42,077
He didn’t say, they had the most knowledge,

75
00:06:42,643 --> 00:06:44,427
he said: They had, the deepest knowledge.

76
00:06:45,308 --> 00:06:47,431
Because there are the people, who came after the Sahabah(صحابه).

77
00:06:47,456 --> 00:06:51,476
Who know things that, the Sahabah(صحابه), may, not, have known.

78
00:06:51,765 --> 00:06:55,743
For example Al-Bukhari(ألبخاريْ), he knew more Ahadith(احاديث) then many of the Sahabah(صحابه).

79
00:06:57,816 --> 00:07:01,180
Why? Because, he knew the Ahadith(احاديث), that Umar(عُمَر) had, he knew the Ahadith(احاديث)

80
00:07:01,205 --> 00:07:03,496
that Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) had, he knew the Ahadith(احاديث) that Uthman(عثمان) had,

81
00:07:03,911 --> 00:07:05,511
he was an encyclopaedia of Hadith(حديث).

82
00:07:06,741 --> 00:07:10,738
When it comes to the opinion of Fiqh(فقه), some of the great Imam(إمام)s of this Ummah(امة)

83
00:07:11,015 --> 00:07:14,902
not only combines the Fiqh(فقه) of one Sahabi(صحابي) but they combine the Fiqh(فقه) of many.

84
00:07:17,707 --> 00:07:20,406
So, Abdullah Ibn Masood(عبد الله بن مسعود) didn’t say that, they had the most knowledge,

85
00:07:20,431 --> 00:07:22,405
he said: They had the deepest knowledge.

86
00:07:22,734 --> 00:07:27,245
So, even though, some of the scholars of Hadith(حديث) or the scholars of Fiqh(فقه),

87
00:07:27,658 --> 00:07:31,108
could know things that some of the Sahabah(صحابه) did not know.

88
00:07:31,704 --> 00:07:32,574
However,

89
00:07:32,898 --> 00:07:37,113
none of the people who came after Sahabah(صحابه), had depth of knowledge that Sahabah(صحابه) had.

90
00:07:37,138 --> 00:07:39,450
They had an edge over everyone of us.

91
00:07:40,219 --> 00:07:42,984
They were there when the Ayaat(آيات) of Qur’an were coming down.

92
00:07:44,166 --> 00:07:46,487
They lived it, they experienced it, first hand.

93
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:51,353
Therefore, everybody, who comes after the Sahabah(صحابه) is just scratching the surface of knowledge

94
00:07:51,668 --> 00:07:53,534
but the Sahabah(صحابه) had the depth of it.

95
00:07:55,353 --> 00:07:59,598
Their understanding was deep and when you have deep understanding,

96
00:08:00,193 --> 00:08:07,568
it makes your outlook to life and your actions better than, somebody who might have more knowledge than you do,

97
00:08:08,737 --> 00:08:13,528
and that's why we should follow the action of the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم

98
00:08:14,288 --> 00:08:16,195
because they had the deepest knowledge.

99
00:08:19,436 --> 00:08:21,007
وَأقَلُهَا تَكَلُفًا

100
00:08:23,150 --> 00:08:25,541
And they were the least superficial

101
00:08:27,924 --> 00:08:32,284
The Sahabah رضي الله عنهم would not act out Islam.

102
00:08:33,750 --> 00:08:38,139
They would not put out fake image. They were not superficial.

103
00:08:38,716 --> 00:08:40,886
They did not pretend to be sophisticated.

104
00:08:41,743 --> 00:08:44,377
You don't know, you have books that are written

105
00:08:45,821 --> 00:08:49,160
and the brother comes and says Masha Allah(ماشاء الله) that was an excellent book,

106
00:08:49,396 --> 00:08:54,829
you know, I read it from the beginning to the end and I didn’t understand it, such a sophisticated book!

107
00:08:55,422 --> 00:08:57,362
 That wasn’t the way of Sahabah رضي الله عنهم .

108
00:08:58,007 --> 00:09:02,364
The way of Sahabah(صحابه) was simplicity, their speeches were short,

109
00:09:03,117 --> 00:09:05,575
their words were concise and clear.

110
00:09:06,606 --> 00:09:11,922
They wouldn’t want to prove that they were knowledgeable by choosing sophisticated long words,

111
00:09:12,446 --> 00:09:15,632
and put it in a rhyming long speech.

112
00:09:16,192 --> 00:09:17,846
Their words were very simple.

113
00:09:18,862 --> 00:09:22,050
Because Sahabah رضي الله عنهم came from a simple background.

114
00:09:23,482 --> 00:09:29,348
The Arabs of Arabia were not adulterated like the other nations of the world.

115
00:09:30,664 --> 00:09:35,636
They were not affected by the luxurious life styles of Persians and Romans.

116
00:09:36,071 --> 00:09:38,502
They were not affected by the philosophy of the Greek.

117
00:09:39,060 --> 00:09:42,008
They were not affected by the theology of the Latins.

118
00:09:42,902 --> 00:09:47,398
The Sahabah رضي الله عنهم most of them were illiterate.

119
00:09:48,417 --> 00:09:51,934
They were very simple and straight forward and honest, decent people.

120
00:09:52,976 --> 00:09:57,707
Even the poetry in time of Jahiliyah(جاهلية) was very simple it wasn’t philosophical.

121
00:09:58,001 --> 00:10:01,793
It was descriptive, they would describe nature, they would describe women,

122
00:10:01,818 --> 00:10:03,496
that was their poetry.

123
00:10:05,456 --> 00:10:11,519
Even the romantic stories that they would mention in their poetry, were very simple.

124
00:10:12,409 --> 00:10:16,554
You compare to Romeo and Juliet and all of that stuff, it's very different.

125
00:10:19,676 --> 00:10:23,116
They were simple in their dress they were simple in their food that they would eat

126
00:10:27,309 --> 00:10:31,011
and that's why, the Fitrah(فطرة) of the Sahabah(صحابه) was very clean.

127
00:10:32,345 --> 00:10:34,431
So, when they accepted Islam,

128
00:10:36,399 --> 00:10:43,981
for them to practice Islam was easy because, Qur’an came on an empty plate.

129
00:10:45,008 --> 00:10:46,775
However, with the other nations,

130
00:10:47,948 --> 00:10:50,081
Qur’an had to cleanse their hearts

131
00:10:50,831 --> 00:10:54,575
Qur’an has to heal the scars, that were left behind by their old life.

132
00:10:55,055 --> 00:10:59,058
Because the Fitrah(فطرة) was deformed, and that's why the Bid’ah(بدعة) ,

133
00:10:59,225 --> 00:11:04,625
the early innovations didn’t start in Makkah and Madina they started among the other nations.

134
00:11:05,164 --> 00:11:09,570
In Iraq(ألعراق) and Ash-Sham(الشام) the nations that were affected by the philosophy of the Greek,

135
00:11:09,595 --> 00:11:14,026
the religious teachings of the other nations.

136
00:11:15,203 --> 00:11:18,284
You know the Arabs in their religion, their religion didn’t have any mythology, like,

137
00:11:18,309 --> 00:11:20,000
for example, like the Hindus or the Greek.

138
00:11:21,306 --> 00:11:26,836
They didn’t have that imagination, they just worship this idle, this stone, this rock,

139
00:11:27,114 --> 00:11:32,493
they would hold on some virtues, truth, chivalry, loyalty

140
00:11:33,146 --> 00:11:37,464
being loyal to their kinship, that was their religion.

141
00:11:37,489 --> 00:11:41,508
So, it wasn’t really religion, it was more of a set of morals

142
00:11:41,668 --> 00:11:44,333
and you just bow down to an idle and you slaughter the animal for it.

143
00:11:45,961 --> 00:11:50,213
Even, their religion was simple, so when they became Muslim,

144
00:11:51,245 --> 00:11:56,658
they carried forward that straight forwardness, honesty and decency.

145
00:11:57,685 --> 00:12:00,312
So, when they became Muslims they straight went to action

146
00:12:00,337 --> 00:12:04,234
they didn’t involved themselves in philosophical, theological discourses.

147
00:12:05,550 --> 00:12:07,429
The Sahabah رضي الله عنهم weren’t into that.

148
00:12:07,909 --> 00:12:12,128
They only came later on in times of the Khilafah(خِلَافَه) of Umar(عُمَر) and Uthman(عثمان) and Ali(علي).

149
00:12:12,873 --> 00:12:15,614
When these other nations were accepting Islam and they were

150
00:12:16,351 --> 00:12:21,024
talking about the issue of Qadr(قدر) and they turned it into a theology.

151
00:12:22,170 --> 00:12:26,421
But Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was on top of them with his stick.

152
00:12:31,998 --> 00:12:33,434
قَوْمُ اُخْتَارَهُمُ الله

153
00:12:33,459 --> 00:12:34,915
Abdullah Ibn Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود) carries on, he says:

154
00:12:34,940 --> 00:12:38,413
قَوْمُ اُخْتَارَهُمُ الله لِصَحْبَةِ نَبِيِّهِ وَإقَامَةِ دِيْنِه

155
00:12:39,750 --> 00:12:46,678
These were the people, whom Allah chose to be companions of His Prophet and to establish His Religion.

156
00:12:46,898 --> 00:12:48,706
 There is a reason, why Allah chose them?

157
00:12:50,102 --> 00:12:53,061
Why Allahعَزّ وجَلّ chose them? Particularly, they were handpicked

158
00:12:53,741 --> 00:12:55,553
to be Sahabah(صحابه) of the greatest Nabi(نَبِي)

159
00:12:56,735 --> 00:12:57,812
لِكُلِّ نَبِّيٍ حَوَارِيْ

160
00:12:57,837 --> 00:13:00,701
Rasool Allah ﷺ says; Every Nabi(نَبِي) has companions.

161
00:13:01,283 --> 00:13:06,795
Allah chose these Sahabah(صحابه) to be companions of Rasool Allah ﷺ for a reason.

162
00:13:09,649 --> 00:13:12,785
Because they were the most fit, for that responsibility.

163
00:13:13,782 --> 00:13:15,554
When Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away,

164
00:13:15,745 --> 00:13:18,750
there was no need to sent any other Nabi(نَبِي) until, the Day of Judgment.

165
00:13:20,176 --> 00:13:23,827
Why? Because the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم can carry it on their own.

166
00:13:29,417 --> 00:13:31,328
So, why are we talking about Sahabah(صحابه)?

167
00:13:31,977 --> 00:13:35,714
Because of these reasons, and also because, Abdullah Ibn Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود) said:

168
00:13:36,126 --> 00:13:37,879
فَإعْرَفُوْا لَهُمْ فَضْلَهُمْ

169
00:13:39,221 --> 00:13:42,164
Recognize their virtues!

170
00:13:42,984 --> 00:13:46,071
We need to recognize the Sahabah(صحابه) for who they are!

171
00:13:47,286 --> 00:13:53,435
We need to put them at high esteem, raise their level, respect them.

172
00:13:54,120 --> 00:14:00,040
So we are coming together now, for entire month to talk about one of the Sahabah(صحابه) Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه

