00:27:37,104 --> 00:27:40,585
In another occasion when he was walking once with some of the Sahabah(صحابه),

339
00:27:40,813 --> 00:27:44,662
he turned around suddenly there was pregnant woman behind him, she had a miscarriage

340
00:27:46,934 --> 00:27:51,013
and the Sahabah(صحابه) were then debating, whether he needs to pay the blood money for that or not

341
00:27:51,054 --> 00:27:55,200
but it happened without his, he didn’t intend to cause her, all of this trouble.

342
00:27:56,075 --> 00:27:58,816
But then Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) said: You need to pay the blood money to her,

343
00:27:58,841 --> 00:28:00,162
because the damage that was done,

344
00:28:00,181 --> 00:28:03,741
but you don’t have to pay it,it should be paid from Bait-Al-Maal(بيت المال) treasury of the Muslims.

345
00:28:05,703 --> 00:28:07,846
When the enemies of Allah, would hear the name of Umar(عُمَر)

346
00:28:08,180 --> 00:28:11,107
their knees would shake and their hearts would tremble.

347
00:28:16,043 --> 00:28:20,368
Now, the unique thing about the personality of Umar(عُمَر) is that,

348
00:28:20,393 --> 00:28:28,571
even though he had all these characteristics, his eyes would flow with tears easily.

349
00:28:30,351 --> 00:28:33,649
And he had very compassionate and merciful heart.

350
00:28:35,409 --> 00:28:40,894
And he was very humble, and that’s the unique thing about personality of Umar(عُمَر).

351
00:28:40,935 --> 00:28:46,292
Usually people, who have this strength tend to be harsh and aggressive and arrogant.

352
00:28:48,217 --> 00:28:51,818
And people who have compassionate and soft heart tend to be weak.

353
00:28:53,219 --> 00:28:55,423
But Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) had these opposing

354
00:28:57,107 --> 00:29:01,260
characteristics in one personality and that’s why he was unique.

355
00:29:05,427 --> 00:29:12,229
His father Al-Khattab Ibn Nufail(الخطاب بن نفيل). His father was a very harsh man,

356
00:29:14,124 --> 00:29:16,108
and Umar(عُمَر) would always remember that.

357
00:29:17,510 --> 00:29:22,196
And Umar(عُمَر) had a tough upbringing. His father was very harsh with him.

358
00:29:23,130 --> 00:29:26,826
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) when he was a Khalifah(خليفه) he would say,

359
00:29:28,123 --> 00:29:36,282
he said: He was with some other companions and he came to this place where he used to be a shepherd,

360
00:29:36,302 --> 00:29:38,745
where he used to takes the camels of his father, he said:

361
00:29:39,064 --> 00:29:44,098
لَا اِلَهَ اِلَّا الله اَلْعَلِيِّ الّعَظِيْمََ اَلْمُعْطِيْ مَا يَشَاءُ لِمَنْ يَشَآءُُ

362
00:29:44,959 --> 00:29:46,639
لَا اِلَهَ اِلَّا الله

363
00:29:46,886 --> 00:29:48,823
The Most High and the Great.

364
00:29:49,385 --> 00:29:51,954
Who gives whatever He wants and to whomever He wants,

365
00:29:52,944 --> 00:29:58,644
I used to be a shepherd for camels of my father in this place,

366
00:30:00,325 --> 00:30:01,674
فِيْ مَدْرَعَةٍ مِّن صُوْفَ

367
00:30:01,784 --> 00:30:04,858
And I would wear, some harsh wool clothes.

368
00:30:06,016 --> 00:30:08,470
وَكَانَ فَظًا يُتْعِبُنِيْ اِذَاعَمِلْتَ

369
00:30:08,903 --> 00:30:12,666
And my father was harsh and he would make me exhausted, when I work

370
00:30:13,468 --> 00:30:15,641
and he would beat me up, if I don’t work.

371
00:30:16,590 --> 00:30:20,698
وَيُضْرِبُنِيْ اِذَا قَصَّرْتََ وَقَدْ اَمْسَيْتُ لَيْسَ بَيْنِيْ وَ بَيْنَ الله اَحَدْ

372
00:30:21,342 --> 00:30:23,831
And today, there is no one between me and Allah.

373
00:30:25,553 --> 00:30:30,913
Being Khalifah(خليفه) of the Muslims on the ladder of classification of humanity, he is the highest.

374
00:30:31,207 --> 00:30:32,564
 There is no one in between him and Allah.

375
00:30:33,600 --> 00:30:35,662
Umar(عُمَر) was saying, Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), there was a day,

376
00:30:35,892 --> 00:30:38,432
when I was a shepherd for my father and he would beat me up.

377
00:30:38,838 --> 00:30:46,421
He would hit me, and he was very harsh with me. And now look at where Umar(عُمَر) is?

378
00:30:47,816 --> 00:30:48,542
So, he used to say;

379
00:30:48,562 --> 00:30:49,221
لا اله الا الله

380
00:30:49,241 --> 00:30:51,094
Allah gives, whatever He wants, to whomever He wants.

381
00:30:51,764 --> 00:30:55,133
Who would imagine that this would be given to Umar(عُمَر), the shepherd of yesterday.

382
00:30:56,534 --> 00:31:01,673
He wasn’t only shepherd for his father but he also use to work for other women, his aunts.

383
00:31:02,382 --> 00:31:14,382
He says, that I had some aunts and I would take their goats or sheep to this valley

384
00:31:15,861 --> 00:31:17,791
and I would come back at the end of the day

385
00:31:17,816 --> 00:31:20,784
and they would give me a handful of raisins or dates.

386
00:31:20,866 --> 00:31:24,485
Now, Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبد الرحمن ابن عوف) is narrating the story,

387
00:31:25,764 --> 00:31:28,740
he said Umar(عُمَر) called the people to the Masjid(مسجد) and when they all assembled

388
00:31:30,385 --> 00:31:35,987
Umar(عُمَر) stands up on the pulpit and he says and this is, when he is Khalifah(خليفه).

389
00:31:36,843 --> 00:31:40,762
He said: I used to be a shepherd for some of my aunts

390
00:31:42,027 --> 00:31:44,016
and I would come back, at the end of the day

391
00:31:45,591 --> 00:31:52,339
and they would give me a handful of dates or raisins and I would have a miserable day.

392
00:31:56,339 --> 00:31:57,797
And then he came down from the pulpit.

393
00:31:59,637 --> 00:32:02,133
I had a miserable day meaning, I worked for my entire day and

394
00:32:02,158 --> 00:32:05,846
this is what I get, handful of dates, that was how poor I was.

395
00:32:08,302 --> 00:32:09,381
Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبد الرحمن ابن عوف) said:

396
00:32:09,415 --> 00:32:11,415
 "مَازِدْتَّ عَلى اَنْ قَمَّئْتَ نَفْسَكْ"

397
00:32:12,318 --> 00:32:16,058
You haven’t done more then to belittle yourself, I mean why, was this your khuttbah(خطبه)?

398
00:32:16,221 --> 00:32:16,781
What's the point?

399
00:32:17,310 --> 00:32:20,743
All what you did is belittle yourself, in front of everyone.

400
00:32:22,699 --> 00:32:23,558
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said:

401
00:32:23,603 --> 00:32:24,639
 "وَيْحَكْ يَا اِبْنِ عَوْفَ"

402
00:32:25,163 --> 00:32:33,044
Woe to you son of ‘Auf(عوف)! My nafs(نفس), myself

403
00:32:34,125 --> 00:32:37,767
was telling me that you are Ameer ul mo'mineen(امير المؤمنين), so who is better than you?

404
00:32:39,184 --> 00:32:43,455
So, I wanted to teach myself a lesson and let it know, who it is.

405
00:32:45,272 --> 00:32:50,129
I wanted myself to know, who it really is, how humble it is,

406
00:32:50,635 --> 00:32:54,554
because myself was trying to play games on me, was trying to tell me that,

407
00:32:55,062 --> 00:32:57,035
I am the Ameer-Ul-Mo'mineen(امير المؤمنين), who is better than me.

408
00:32:59,785 --> 00:33:05,221
When we are going through the story of Umar(عُمَر), I wanted to reflect on his sayings, and his actions.

409
00:33:05,287 --> 00:33:07,338
 Because it tells you allot about his personality.

410
00:33:08,810 --> 00:33:13,450
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب), he cannot be fooled by anyone including his own self.

411
00:33:15,330 --> 00:33:18,072
See, his self was trying to play games on him

412
00:33:18,803 --> 00:33:22,700
and it was telling him that you are the best. Look at who you are?

413
00:33:24,996 --> 00:33:29,290
Brothers and sisters Shaytan(شيطان) cannot come to you unless you allow him to do so!

414
00:33:34,707 --> 00:33:37,758
On the Day of Judgment people would go to the Shaytan(شيطان) and complain

415
00:33:37,783 --> 00:33:38,625
and Shaytan(شيطان) will say;

416
00:33:38,705 --> 00:33:40,293
"مَا كَانَ  لِيْ عَلَيْكُمْ مِنْ سُلْطَانْ"

417
00:33:40,632 --> 00:33:42,948
I had no authority over you, you are the ones,

418
00:33:43,038 --> 00:33:44,198
"كُنْتُمْ قَوْمً طَاغِيْنَ"

419
00:33:44,341 --> 00:33:45,974
But you are people who are transgressors.

420
00:33:47,346 --> 00:33:51,059
Shaytan(شيطان) cannot have access to your heart unless you give him the keys.

421
00:33:52,524 --> 00:33:55,694
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was closing all of the cracks

422
00:33:56,620 --> 00:33:58,421
which would allow Shaytan(شيطان) to come in.

423
00:33:58,784 --> 00:34:03,102
While we don’t have just cracks, we have opened our gates,

424
00:34:03,951 --> 00:34:07,232
the gates of our heart to Shaytan(شيطان). Welcome "come in".

425
00:34:08,251 --> 00:34:10,682
Shaytan(شيطان) cannot come to you unless you allow him to.

426
00:34:11,877 --> 00:34:13,736
When he went to Adam عليه السّلام in Jannah(جنة).

427
00:34:13,988 --> 00:34:17,512
What did he tell the Adam(آدم)? Did he tell him go and eat from the tree Allah has banned?

428
00:34:18,068 --> 00:34:19,768
Go and eat from the tree that is Haram(حرام)?

429
00:34:19,914 --> 00:34:21,748
Go and disobey Allahعَزّ وجَلّ?

430
00:34:22,041 --> 00:34:22,561
No!

431
00:34:23,101 --> 00:34:23,868
He told him:

432
00:34:23,980 --> 00:34:28,342
يَا آدَمْ هَلْ اَدُلُّكَ عَلَى شَّجَرَةِ الّخُلْدِ وَمُلْكِ لَا يَبْلَىً۞

433
00:34:28,636 --> 00:34:32,331
O Adam(آدم) I am going to tell you about

434
00:34:32,792 --> 00:34:36,507
a tree that would give you everlasting life and a great kingdom.

435
00:34:37,461 --> 00:34:41,835
Shaytan(شيطان) knows what is appealing to our hearts. You want to live forever,

436
00:34:42,069 --> 00:34:47,485
you want to have power, so these are the gates in which he came in heart of Adam عليه السّلام.

437
00:34:48,588 --> 00:34:51,510
So, Shaytan(شيطان) needs to find the way to come in

438
00:34:51,725 --> 00:34:55,902
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was sealing all these cracks. He shuts them,

439
00:34:57,558 --> 00:34:58,472
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) says:

440
00:34:58,551 --> 00:35:00,559
"لَسْتُ بِالْخِبِّ وَلَااَلْخِبِّ يَخْدَعْنِيْ"

441
00:35:01,884 --> 00:35:05,931
I am not a deceiver, nor would I allow anybody to deceive me.

442
00:35:06,865 --> 00:35:10,516
I don’t go around deceiving people but in the same time, no one can deceive me.

443
00:35:11,402 --> 00:35:16,193
That’s why Rasool Allah ﷺ says; Whenever, Shaytan(شيطان) sees you following one road,

444
00:35:17,158 --> 00:35:19,876
he would take another. Shaytan(شيطان) has given up on Umar(عُمَر) there is no hope,

445
00:35:20,215 --> 00:35:22,244
there is no way, it's just a waste of time.

446
00:35:27,115 --> 00:35:36,803
So, the father of Umar(عُمَر), was very rough and harsh in the way, he use to bring up his children.

447
00:35:41,029 --> 00:35:42,237
The mother of Umar(عُمَر),

448
00:35:44,220 --> 00:35:48,087
there is one opinion that says that she is from the family of Bani Makhzom(بني مخزوم),

449
00:35:48,303 --> 00:35:49,699
the family of Khaalid Ibn Waleed(خالد ابن وليد)

450
00:35:50,577 --> 00:35:54,187
but most of the historians says that she is the cousin of Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل),

451
00:35:55,027 --> 00:35:56,554
she is the cousin of Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل).

452
00:35:56,579 --> 00:36:01,059
Hintimah bint Hisham(حنتمه بنت هشام), Her name is Hintimah bint Hisham(حنتمه بنت هشام).

453
00:36:02,948 --> 00:36:06,549
His Wives! He married seven or eight in total.

454
00:36:07,615 --> 00:36:09,681
He married Zainab Bint Madh’oon(زينب بنت مظعون),

455
00:36:09,903 --> 00:36:13,217
the sister of great Sahaabi(صحابي) Uthman Ibn Madh’oon(عثمان بن مظعون).

456
00:36:13,861 --> 00:36:16,347
He married her during the time of Jahiliyah(جاهليه)

457
00:36:16,607 --> 00:36:21,288
and she was the mother of Abdullah(عبدالله), Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) the eldest, and Hafsa(حفصه).

458
00:36:22,875 --> 00:36:25,340
He married Maleeka Bint Jarwal(مليكه بنت جرول) ,

459
00:36:25,776 --> 00:36:28,937
and she was the mother of Obaidullah(عبيد الله), and he divorced her.

460
00:36:30,431 --> 00:36:34,930
He married Quraiba Bint Abi Makhzom(قُريبَه بنت ابي مخزوم), and he later on divorced her

461
00:36:35,148 --> 00:36:39,383
and she then married Abdur Rahman Ibn Abi Bakr(عبد الرحمن ابن ابي بكر).

462
00:36:41,414 --> 00:36:43,769
He married Umm Hakeem Bint Al-Harris(ام حكيم بنت الحارث),

463
00:36:44,826 --> 00:36:47,925
she was the wife of Ikramah Ibn Abi Jahal(عكرمة بن ابي جهل),

464
00:36:48,539 --> 00:36:51,453
when Ikramah(عكرمة) died in the Battle of Yarmook(يرموك),

465
00:36:51,791 --> 00:36:54,101
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عُمرإبن خطاب) married her.

466
00:36:54,625 --> 00:37:01,426
And then when Umar(عُمَر) died she then, remarried again. She was the mother of Fatimah(فاطمه).

467
00:37:02,272 --> 00:37:05,764
He married Jameela bint Asim bin Sabit(جميله بنت عاصم بن ثابت).

468
00:37:06,399 --> 00:37:09,714
He married ‘Atika bint Zayd Bin ‘Amr Bin Nufail(عاتكة بنت زيد بن عمرو بن نفيل),

469
00:37:10,654 --> 00:37:11,931
she was a relative of his.

470
00:37:12,944 --> 00:37:15,707
She was married before him to Abdullah Ibn Abi Bakr(عبدالله ابن ابي بكر).

471
00:37:16,402 --> 00:37:22,254
And when Umar(عُمَر) was killed, then she married Zubair Ibn Awam(زبير بن عوام).

472
00:37:23,458 --> 00:37:25,963
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) wanted to marry

473
00:37:26,613 --> 00:37:30,659
the youngest daughter of Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) her name is Umm Kalthoom(ام كلثوم)

474
00:37:30,684 --> 00:37:35,434
she was born, after Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) passed away, she was his youngest.

475
00:37:36,392 --> 00:37:41,213
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) asked for her hand in marriage, she refused.

476
00:37:42,687 --> 00:37:43,321
Ayesha(عائشه) told her:

477
00:37:43,356 --> 00:37:45,022
 "أَ تَرْ غَبِيْنَ عَنْ اَمِيْرُ الّمُؤمِنِيْنْ"

478
00:37:45,121 --> 00:37:46,774
You don’t want to marry Ameer-ul-Mo'mineen(امير المؤمنين)?

479
00:37:47,277 --> 00:37:47,641
She said:

480
00:37:47,709 --> 00:37:49,209
"اِنَّ هُوْ خَشِنِ ا لْعَيْشْ"

481
00:37:50,325 --> 00:37:54,240
His life style is harsh. Women want an easy life style.

482
00:37:54,807 --> 00:38:01,123
Even in those days, she wants her husband to take care of her, make her life comfortable and easy.

483
00:38:01,148 --> 00:38:02,598
So she said: I do not want him.

484
00:38:04,403 --> 00:38:06,742
So, Ayesha(عائشه) told, Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) about it.

485
00:38:06,834 --> 00:38:09,159
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) went to Umar(عُمَر) and said:

486
00:38:09,991 --> 00:38:13,772
I have a suggestion for you, why don’t you marry Umm Kalthoom(ام كلثوم) the daughter of Ali(علي)?

487
00:38:14,449 --> 00:38:16,455
Because by marrying her you will have,

488
00:38:17,356 --> 00:38:19,077
ثَبِّبْ اِلى رَسُولِ الله

489
00:38:20,057 --> 00:38:22,961
You will have a relationship into the family of Rasool Ullah

490
00:38:23,168 --> 00:38:25,066
because Umm Kalthoom(ام كلثوم) was daughter of Fatima(فاطمه).

491
00:38:25,091 --> 00:38:28,321
So she was the grand-daughter of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

492
00:38:29,723 --> 00:38:33,221
So Umar(عُمَر) asked for her hand in marriage and she agreed and he married her.

493
00:38:34,350 --> 00:38:36,188
That was the daughter of Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب).

494
00:38:37,996 --> 00:38:42,970
Now, Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) was much younger than Umar(عُمَر), so his daughter was very young.

495
00:38:48,561 --> 00:38:52,449
Lohaiya(لوحَيَّهْ) was either a slave girl or wife, there is a difference of opinion

496
00:38:53,290 --> 00:38:56,010
and she bore him, Abdur Rahman(عبد الرحمن), the youngest.

497
00:38:56,731 --> 00:39:03,489
And then he had a slave girl her name was Fuqiyha(فُقَيْهَة) and she was the mother of Zainab(زينب).

498
00:39:04,441 --> 00:39:08,183
So, he had a total of thirteen children from his marriages.

499
00:39:08,522 --> 00:39:10,761
Zayd(زيد) the eldest and Zayd(زيد) the youngest

500
00:39:10,786 --> 00:39:13,895
I am translating literally Zaid Al-Akbar(زيد الاكبر) and Zaid Al-Asghar(زيد الاصغر),

501
00:39:14,334 --> 00:39:17,478
he named two of his sons Zayd(زيد) because his brother was Zayd(زيد).

502
00:39:18,121 --> 00:39:22,832
He named him on his brother Zayd Bin Khattab(زيد بن ألخطاب), Whom he use to love very much,

503
00:39:23,413 --> 00:39:25,513
 it's his elder brother, who died as a Shaheed(شهيد).

504
00:39:26,180 --> 00:39:30,043
He had Asim(عاصم), Abdullah(عبدالله), and then Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) the Eldest,

505
00:39:30,068 --> 00:39:32,106
then Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) the Middle and then Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) the Youngest.

506
00:39:32,327 --> 00:39:36,112
So he used to love the name Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) he named three of his kids Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن)

507
00:39:36,576 --> 00:39:37,396
Abdur Rahman Al-Akbar(عبدالرحمن الاكبر),

508
00:39:37,462 --> 00:39:38,452
Abdur Rahman Al-Awsat(عبدالرحمن الاوسط)

509
00:39:38,559 --> 00:39:39,424
 Abdur Rahman Al-Asghar(عبدالرحمن الاصغر).

510
00:39:41,176 --> 00:39:46,404
He had Obaidallah(عبيدالله) and Ayaz(عياض), these are the male children.

511
00:39:46,673 --> 00:39:52,222
Then he had four daughters, Hafsa(حفصه), Ruqiya(رقيه), Zaynab(زينب) and Fatima(فاطمه), a total of thirteen.

512
00:39:53,304 --> 00:39:55,697
Just a word on the marriages in those days,

513
00:39:55,755 --> 00:39:58,708
because some thoughts may have come up in your mind,

514
00:39:58,729 --> 00:40:00,054
when we were talking about the marriages of Umar(عمر)

515
00:40:00,436 --> 00:40:02,518
first of all you noticed he married more than four,

516
00:40:02,892 --> 00:40:05,980
obviously, he didn’t have more than four at any one point.

517
00:40:06,865 --> 00:40:13,917
We are talking about total number of women that he married during his life time were seven or eight.

518
00:40:14,718 --> 00:40:19,077
You would also noticed that, he divorced two of his wives and he divorced them in Islam.

519
00:40:19,102 --> 00:40:20,990
It's was not in the time of Jahiliyah(جاهليه).

520
00:40:21,016 --> 00:40:22,503
Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) also divorced,

521
00:40:24,609 --> 00:40:27,409
Rasool Allah ﷺ, was almost going to divorce.

522
00:40:27,589 --> 00:40:29,109
Many of the Sahabah(صحابه) divorced.

523
00:40:29,333 --> 00:40:32,465
Now a days, we tend to see divorce as un-acceptable thing.

524
00:40:32,766 --> 00:40:37,611
In fact, when we talk about the ills of society, we say the ratio of divorce is so high.

525
00:40:37,961 --> 00:40:39,012
Well if that’s the standard,

526
00:40:39,588 --> 00:40:42,988
then the ratio of divorce in the time of Sahabah(صحابه) was extremely high.

527
00:40:44,781 --> 00:40:47,928
So, that’s not really a criteria of the health of society.

528
00:40:50,602 --> 00:40:53,507
But their perception of divorce was different than ours.

529
00:40:54,604 --> 00:40:58,487
They used to see marriage as a relationship between two souls,

530
00:40:58,808 --> 00:41:00,380
so there needs to be a compatibility.

531
00:41:01,362 --> 00:41:05,716
If it doesn’t work out it's just like a business agreement if it doesn’t work out then fine

532
00:41:06,070 --> 00:41:07,070
we can part.

533
00:41:08,221 --> 00:41:10,587
Now a days, we see divorce in a different light.

534
00:41:11,583 --> 00:41:14,172
We see it, as a something that is a "No, No, you never do."

535
00:41:14,723 --> 00:41:16,247
And then if it ever happens,

536
00:41:16,272 --> 00:41:20,952
thats the stigma on the person until the end of their life especially to the women.

537
00:41:21,672 --> 00:41:28,463
A woman who is divorced, no one wants to marry her and that is very unfair, that’s oppressive.

538
00:41:30,169 --> 00:41:33,446
You've noticed in the time of Sahabah رضي الله عنهم,

539
00:41:33,722 --> 00:41:35,855
no woman would be left without a husband.

540
00:41:37,313 --> 00:41:42,974
Because for a Muslim male or female, family is the essence of your life,

541
00:41:44,391 --> 00:41:46,219
family is the most important thing you have.

542
00:41:47,511 --> 00:41:50,967
Your family as a Muslim is very, very important.

543
00:41:51,838 --> 00:41:55,658
We not living a life style of Kuffar(كفار), if you don’t have a maid that’s fine,

544
00:41:55,848 --> 00:42:00,608
you go from one pub to another and enjoy yourself. That’s not a life style of a Muslim.

545
00:42:02,215 --> 00:42:05,662
The Kuffar(كفار) women that survive changing from one hand to another,

546
00:42:06,409 --> 00:42:10,235
living a life that’s closer to the animal life, then is to human life.

547
00:42:14,104 --> 00:42:17,888
So, for a Muslim man or a woman family is everything.

548
00:42:20,518 --> 00:42:24,072
So the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم would never leave any of their sisters,

549
00:42:24,310 --> 00:42:27,528
without the opportunity and privilege, of being married.

550
00:42:29,048 --> 00:42:32,710
And that’s why polygamy was very wide spread and it was accepted.

551
00:42:33,120 --> 00:42:34,906
And if a woman or a man divorced

552
00:42:36,165 --> 00:42:38,660
that’s not a stigma on them, they can easily remarried.

553
00:42:41,298 --> 00:42:46,249
Also you would find that, there could be a great difference in the age.

554
00:42:47,050 --> 00:42:50,842
As long as both sides agree, there wasn’t a cultural problem with that

555
00:42:50,867 --> 00:42:54,555
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was very old when he married Umm Kalthoom Bint Ali(ام كلثوم بنت علي).

556
00:42:55,224 --> 00:42:59,210
And Umm Kalthoom bint Abu Bakr(ام كلثوم بنت ابو بكر) didn’t refuse to marry him

557
00:42:59,235 --> 00:43:03,978
because he was old because she then married Talha Ibn Obaidullah(طلحه ابن عبيد الله), who was also old.

558
00:43:05,923 --> 00:43:09,972
So, as long as both sides agree they were fine with it, culturally.

559
00:43:10,772 --> 00:43:14,502
So, our perception of marriage and divorce is different than the perception of the Sahabah(صحابه).

560
00:43:15,252 --> 00:43:17,654
In times of Sahabah(صحابه) marriage was early and easy

561
00:43:19,515 --> 00:43:24,383
and everyone was allowed to be part of a family.

562
00:43:26,058 --> 00:43:28,960
Now, there are millions of women around the Muslim world,

563
00:43:28,985 --> 00:43:30,382
it's not really a problem in the west

564
00:43:30,816 --> 00:43:33,793
but in the Muslim countries it’s a disastrous social problem.

565
00:43:34,263 --> 00:43:39,433
Millions of women are growing older and older and they cannot get married.

566
00:43:40,500 --> 00:43:43,312
Why? Because nobody wants to marry them, when they are old,

567
00:43:43,602 --> 00:43:46,309
nobody wants to allow polygamy,

568
00:43:48,113 --> 00:43:50,544
and that’s why we have all these women, who are unmarried.

569
00:44:02,074 --> 00:44:04,119
So, when you look at it from this point of view,

570
00:44:04,943 --> 00:44:08,157
polygamy is fairness to woman, rather than being oppressive.

571
00:44:08,919 --> 00:44:13,509
Because it, then gives every women in the society an opportunity to be married,

572
00:44:13,534 --> 00:44:15,230
because always women are more than men.

573
00:44:16,953 --> 00:44:20,226
So, if polygamy is not accepted then that means there are going to be women,

574
00:44:20,247 --> 00:44:23,092
who will not be able to get married.

575
00:44:24,224 --> 00:44:33,277
So, the champions of women's rights, should actually be asking for the legalization of polygamy.

576
00:44:37,649 --> 00:44:39,889
The Work Of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرإبن خطاب).

577
00:44:39,956 --> 00:44:46,534
His first profession was, being a shepherd for his father and for his aunts.

578
00:44:47,380 --> 00:44:52,261
And then he started a business. And he was very successful at it,

579
00:44:52,566 --> 00:44:56,851
he would travel to Syria, and to Yemen and trade, and he became very wealthy.

580
00:44:56,972 --> 00:45:02,735
He became one of the wealthy men of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ). And also he was a wrestler.

581
00:45:03,133 --> 00:45:07,550
That’s something he used to, join in competition in Souq Akaaz(سوق عكاظ)

582
00:45:09,131 --> 00:45:10,511
and he was unbeatable.

583
00:45:12,935 --> 00:45:14,935
In Jahiliyah(جاهليه) because of the nature of the Umar(عُمَر),

584
00:45:14,960 --> 00:45:19,483
Umar(عُمَر) was not a person who would do something with a half hearted effort.

585
00:45:21,349 --> 00:45:23,422
He would go full throttle into everything.

586
00:45:24,693 --> 00:45:32,241
He was very committed, disciplined person and he would go ahead with what he believes.

587
00:45:32,526 --> 00:45:36,610
He doesn’t sit on the side lines on the margins, he would get involved.

588
00:45:37,122 --> 00:45:45,090
Therefore, in Jahiliyah(جاهليه), he was one of the most effective men of the Quraish(قريش)

589
00:45:46,004 --> 00:45:48,187
in the inquisition against the Muslims.

590
00:45:50,316 --> 00:45:53,387
He was one of toughest in his persecution of the Muslims.

591
00:45:53,781 --> 00:45:57,615
Because that’s the nature of the Umar(عُمَر), he goes full ahead with what he believes,

592
00:45:58,307 --> 00:45:59,355
he don’t sit on the sidelines.

593
00:46:00,383 --> 00:46:03,588
So, he used to torment, he used to torture, this slave girl.

594
00:46:04,564 --> 00:46:06,596
He would lash her with this whip

595
00:46:07,905 --> 00:46:11,694
and then when he would get tired he would sit down, and what would he tell her:

596
00:46:11,845 --> 00:46:12,603
He would tell her; "Listen!

597
00:46:12,914 --> 00:46:16,007
I didn’t stop because I feel sorry for you, I stopped because, I am tired."

598
00:46:18,934 --> 00:46:22,310
She would respond back and say: "It is Allah, who made you stop,"

599
00:46:23,568 --> 00:46:26,184
that’s the Eeman(ايمان) of this slave.

600
00:46:29,259 --> 00:46:36,235
And it was unacceptable to the minds of many of the Muslims that one day Umar(عُمَر) could become Muslim.

601
00:46:38,943 --> 00:46:43,609
One day when Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was walking down in the streets of Makkah,

602
00:46:43,649 --> 00:46:50,306
he saw one of the Sahaabiyaat(صحابيات), who was on her way to Abyssinia.

603
00:46:51,076 --> 00:46:52,653
She was making a Hijrah(هجرة) to Al-Habasha(اَلْحَبَشَه).

604
00:46:54,656 --> 00:46:59,216
So, Umar(عُمَر) said: Are you leaving?. She said: Yes!

605
00:47:00,470 --> 00:47:04,129
Because you have oppressed us, and persecuted us.

606
00:47:04,971 --> 00:47:10,687
We are going to travel in the land of Allah in order that we can practice our Religion freely.

607
00:47:12,554 --> 00:47:14,742
What did Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) say? He said:

608
00:47:17,118 --> 00:47:18,400
صَحِبَكُمُ الله,

609
00:47:18,938 --> 00:47:21,718
May Allah be with you!

610
00:47:23,511 --> 00:47:26,410
This statement was contrary to the nature of Umar(عُمَر).

611
00:47:27,219 --> 00:47:29,705
Umar(عُمَر) showing compassion to a Muslim?

612
00:47:31,824 --> 00:47:36,811
So, when No'aim Ibn Abdullah(نُعَيْم ابن عبدالله) came back he was with the Sahaabiya(صحابية).

613
00:47:38,703 --> 00:47:40,033
She told him what happened.

614
00:47:42,130 --> 00:47:47,336
He said: It appears that you are hoping for Umar(عُمَر) to become a Muslim?

615
00:47:47,944 --> 00:47:50,210
She said: Yes! He said: Let me tell you,

616
00:47:50,871 --> 00:47:54,303
"The donkey of his father would become a Muslim, before he does".

617
00:47:56,172 --> 00:47:58,514
He is telling her that you women go with your emotions,

618
00:47:58,539 --> 00:48:01,444
Umar(عُمَر) is not going to become a Muslim.

619
00:48:01,822 --> 00:48:03,645
But she was right and he was wrong.

620
00:48:04,735 --> 00:48:06,116
But this is to show you that,

621
00:48:06,963 --> 00:48:10,620
they didn’t see it possible that one day this man could become a Muslim.

622
00:48:11,422 --> 00:48:12,972
But Hidayah(هدايه) is in the hands of Allaah.

623
00:48:14,219 --> 00:48:15,585
You never know who's going to embrace it.

624
00:48:17,580 --> 00:48:19,608
It is so far fetched, of an idea.

625
00:48:19,913 --> 00:48:23,680
He thought that donkey would become muslim before he does.

626
00:48:26,091 --> 00:48:27,929
For them it was out of their minds.

627
00:48:32,013 --> 00:48:33,970
HOW DID HE BECOME MUSLIM?

628
00:48:36,014 --> 00:48:39,850
There was one incident that was narrated by his son Abdullah(عبدالله).

629
00:48:41,300 --> 00:48:49,062
He said: One day a handsome man walked in front of us, so my father looked at him.

630
00:48:49,201 --> 00:48:53,239
He looked at his face and he said: If my intuition is right

631
00:48:54,447 --> 00:48:59,665
this man was a Kaahin(كاهن), a fortune teller for his people.

632
00:49:02,238 --> 00:49:06,290
This is what you call, a Farasa(فراسة), Farasa(فراسة) is the art of reading the face

633
00:49:06,381 --> 00:49:10,247
and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) had that ability; it’s a gift from Allah.

634
00:49:10,651 --> 00:49:14,252
You look at the face of some body and you read their personality.

635
00:49:15,178 --> 00:49:16,601
And Umar(عُمَر) was good at Farasa(فراسة).

636
00:49:18,028 --> 00:49:21,418
So, by just looking at face of this man he never met him before,

637
00:49:21,921 --> 00:49:26,886
he read his face and he said: This man used to be fortune teller of his people,

638
00:49:27,746 --> 00:49:32,953
so they called the man, and he said: I have never seen something like this before,

639
00:49:33,316 --> 00:49:37,082
he was amazed. Umar(عُمَر) told him to tell me about yourself.

640
00:49:39,586 --> 00:49:43,880
By the way, this issue of Farasa(فراسة) was seen as an art.

641
00:49:43,905 --> 00:49:46,322
They say that Ash-Shafi'e(الشافعي) went to Yemen to learn Farasa(فراسة).

642
00:49:46,347 --> 00:49:48,742
So, its some kind of art that could be taught,

643
00:49:49,196 --> 00:49:52,467
and it appears in some kind of cultures like for example Chinese culture,

644
00:49:52,956 --> 00:49:56,200
they have some sort of different version of Farasa(فراسة), reading the face.

645
00:49:57,352 --> 00:49:58,572
But Rasool Allah ﷺ says:

646
00:49:58,624 --> 00:50:00,824
 "إِتَّقُوْا فَرَاسَةِ الْمُؤمِنْ فَإِنَه’ يَرَى بِنُوْرِ الله"

647
00:50:01,538 --> 00:50:05,939
Beware of the Farasa(فراسة) of believer because he can see by the light of Allah.

648
00:50:08,529 --> 00:50:11,096
So it is a gift that is given to some people and Umar(عُمَر) had it.

649
00:50:11,615 --> 00:50:16,293
So, Umar(عُمَر) called the man and the man said: Yes! I was the fortune teller of my people.

650
00:50:19,358 --> 00:50:23,993
Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عمر) said: Rarely, would the intuition of my father go wrong.

651
00:50:25,366 --> 00:50:26,507
It was always on target.

652
00:50:28,721 --> 00:50:33,363
So, Umar(عُمَر) told him tell me the strangest thing that your Jinn(جن) told you.

653
00:50:33,637 --> 00:50:37,309
Because these are the people, the fortune tellers deal with Jinn(جن)

654
00:50:38,023 --> 00:50:39,549
they were dealing with Jinn(جن).

655
00:50:40,055 --> 00:50:44,171
So Umar(عُمَر) is asking him, tell me about strangest thing that you heard from your Jinn(جن)?

656
00:50:44,667 --> 00:50:50,419
So, he said my Jinn(جن) came to me, he mentions this rhyming words.

657
00:50:52,097 --> 00:50:54,103
Speaking about coming of a prophet.

658
00:50:55,661 --> 00:50:57,756
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: Yes! That’s true.

659
00:50:58,175 --> 00:51:03,637
One day, when a man was sacrificing for the idols next to Al-Ka’aba(ألكعبه),

660
00:51:04,353 --> 00:51:06,245
I heard a very loud voice.

661
00:51:08,654 --> 00:51:12,437
And this voice was saying something similar there is a prophet, who is coming

662
00:51:12,997 --> 00:51:16,719
and then Umar(عمر) said: Immediately after that Muhammadﷺ claimed to be a Prophet.

663
00:51:18,010 --> 00:51:22,182
So, these were hints, that were coming to Umar(عُمَر) to prepare him.

664
00:51:22,913 --> 00:51:26,582
To prepare him, for Islam, so this was the thing that happened in the beginning.

665
00:51:31,939 --> 00:51:37,033
Another important incident was what happened between him and this Sahaabiya(صحابيه)

666
00:51:37,054 --> 00:51:40,513
when his heart was feeling soft, you can see that he was getting closer to Islam,

667
00:51:40,929 --> 00:51:42,228
his stance was changing.

668
00:51:46,406 --> 00:51:55,379
One day while the Mushrikeen(مشركين) were discussing how to deal with the problem of Muhammadﷺ?

669
00:51:57,418 --> 00:51:59,553
They said: Who will volunteer to kill him?

670
00:52:01,236 --> 00:52:04,412
Umar(عُمَر) said: I will! They said: You are the one for it.

671
00:52:06,142 --> 00:52:11,695
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) carries his sword, in the middle of very hot day in Makkah.

672
00:52:12,594 --> 00:52:16,522
And he was walking down the streets towards Daar Ul Arqam(دار الارقم),

673
00:52:16,543 --> 00:52:19,029
he was told that Rasool Allah ﷺ is meeting there.

674
00:52:20,708 --> 00:52:25,150
And this is after, many of Sahabah(صحابه) have already made Hijrah(هجرة) to Abyssinia,

675
00:52:25,748 --> 00:52:28,744
so Rasool Allah ﷺ was left with small group of a Sahabah(صحابه),

676
00:52:28,769 --> 00:52:33,709
Hamza Ibn Abdul Muttalib(حمزة بن عبدالمطلب), Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, and few other Sahabah(صحابه).

677
00:52:34,333 --> 00:52:38,228
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was heading straight down in the streets of Makkah,

678
00:52:38,535 --> 00:52:40,767
and you can see evil in his eyes.

679
00:52:45,758 --> 00:52:49,562
So, one of the companions, who was practicing Islam in secret

680
00:52:51,028 --> 00:52:54,718
saw Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) and he realized that there was something wrong.

681
00:52:55,750 --> 00:52:59,101
So, he told him where are you heading?

682
00:53:00,004 --> 00:53:05,905
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: To this man, who has disunited our people,

683
00:53:07,534 --> 00:53:14,456
and who has made fools out of us, and who has cursed our gods, I am going to kill him.

684
00:53:19,191 --> 00:53:26,704
So, the companion told him: It seems that you are, too confident in yourself.

685
00:53:27,780 --> 00:53:30,958
Do you think that Bani Abd Manaf(بنى عبد مناف), the family of Rasool Ullah

686
00:53:31,618 --> 00:53:35,233
are going to let you walk on the face of the earth, after you killed their man?

687
00:53:37,027 --> 00:53:38,257
It was a tribal system.

688
00:53:40,365 --> 00:53:43,903
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was upset so, they started an argument.

689
00:53:45,008 --> 00:53:49,225
And then Umar(عُمَر) told this man, he said: I think that you have became Muslim,

690
00:53:49,266 --> 00:53:54,623
if I am sure, that you are Muslim I am going to start by killing you first.

691
00:53:58,063 --> 00:54:05,855
So, the Sahabi(صحابي) felt that, the whole reason, why this Sahabi(صحابي) was discussing with Umar(عمر)

692
00:54:05,880 --> 00:54:11,046
is because he wants to divert him from his objective. He wants to save Rasool Ullah.

693
00:54:11,234 --> 00:54:14,361
So, when he felt that, there is no hope,

694
00:54:15,535 --> 00:54:21,279
in carry on this discussion with Umar(عمر) in this way, he told Umar(عمر):

695
00:54:22,175 --> 00:54:26,180
Well before you go to Rasool Allah ﷺ why don’t you take care of your house hold first?

696
00:54:26,411 --> 00:54:28,688
Why don’t you take care of your house hold first?

697
00:54:29,911 --> 00:54:31,574
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: What did you mean?

698
00:54:32,239 --> 00:54:36,649
He said: Your sister and her husband, they have became Muslim.

699
00:54:40,144 --> 00:54:46,448
This Sahabi(صحابي) only said this, when every other argument did not work.

700
00:54:47,881 --> 00:54:53,603
The sister of Umar(عُمَر) was Muslim in secret and so was her husband Saeed Ibn Zayd(سعيد بن زيد).

701
00:54:55,436 --> 00:55:01,606
What the Sahabi(صحابي) did? Was put the sister of Umar(عمر) and her husband in a big trouble.

702
00:55:02,160 --> 00:55:09,824
He exposed them. But, why would he do that? He did that to save Rasool Allah ﷺ.

703
00:55:11,046 --> 00:55:19,191
So, it shows you everything and anything can be sacrificed for the safety of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

704
00:55:21,153 --> 00:55:21,651
 Everything!!!

705
00:55:23,926 --> 00:55:29,994
So, now Umar(عُمَر) changed his coarse and he went straight to the house of his sister.

706
00:55:31,021 --> 00:55:35,530
When he got next to the door, he heard them reciting Qur’an.

707
00:55:37,323 --> 00:55:40,281
Fatimah Bint Al-Khattab(فاطمه بنت خطاب) and her husband Saeed Bin Zayd(سعيد بن زيد).

708
00:55:40,306 --> 00:55:42,576
Saeed Bin Zayd(سعيد بن زيد) is the cousin of Umar(عمر).

709
00:55:43,112 --> 00:55:45,879
And he is one of the ten, who were given the glad tidings of Jannah(جنة).

710
00:55:46,703 --> 00:55:51,684
and they were being taught Qur’an by Khabaab Ibn Al-Arat(خباب ابن الارت).

711
00:55:54,048 --> 00:55:57,351
When he knocked the door and they saw that it's Umar(عمر)

712
00:55:58,279 --> 00:56:00,562
Khabaab(خباب) immediately, went into hiding

713
00:56:01,229 --> 00:56:05,457
and Fatima(فاطمه), she hide the Scroll of Qur’an under her thigh.

714
00:56:07,679 --> 00:56:12,228
Umar(عُمَر) came in and he said: What was that humming sound that I heard?

715
00:56:12,960 --> 00:56:17,578
They said: It was nothing we were just talking. He said: Don’t lie to me.

716
00:56:17,964 --> 00:56:23,437
What was that noise and have you became Muslims?

717
00:56:25,177 --> 00:56:28,704
Saeed Bin Zayd(سعيد بن زيد) said: Well what if Islam is better than your religion?

718
00:56:29,846 --> 00:56:33,041
At that point Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) attacked Saeed(سعيد),

719
00:56:33,842 --> 00:56:38,015
he threw him to the ground and then he sat on top of him.

720
00:56:40,892 --> 00:56:43,885
When Fatima(فاطمه) saw that, she came to defend her husband.

721
00:56:44,576 --> 00:56:50,573
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), he struck her and it came on her face and she started to bleed.

722
00:56:53,311 --> 00:57:01,428
She then said: You enemy of Allah, you hit me just because, I believed in Allah?

723
00:57:03,171 --> 00:57:05,928
Whether you like it or not,

724
00:57:08,128 --> 00:57:11,512
I bear witness and I testify that there is no god but Allah

725
00:57:11,537 --> 00:57:14,857
and that Muhammadﷺ is Messenger of Allah, Do whatever you want!

726
00:57:17,612 --> 00:57:20,780
When Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) saw this strength emanating from his sister

727
00:57:20,805 --> 00:57:24,556
and this confidence and he saw that blood on her face.

728
00:57:25,083 --> 00:57:27,275
He regretted what he has done,

729
00:57:27,795 --> 00:57:32,758
it was unacceptable in their customs to hit a woman in such a manner.

730
00:57:34,164 --> 00:57:36,716
So, he felt sorry for what he did to his sister.

731
00:57:38,354 --> 00:57:43,669
So he moved away from Saeed(سعيد) and he sat down.

732
00:57:44,470 --> 00:57:50,025
He said: Hand me over your scrolls. She said: I won’t!

733
00:57:50,754 --> 00:57:55,816
Umar(عُمَر) said: What you said, has struck a chord in my heart

734
00:57:56,899 --> 00:58:00,988
and I promise you that, I will return the scrolls to you safely.

735
00:58:02,626 --> 00:58:06,708
She said: You are a Mushrik(مشرك) and you are in state of impurity,

736
00:58:07,212 --> 00:58:09,085
- so you have to make Ghussal(غسل) first.

737
00:58:10,511 --> 00:58:15,817
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) went and he made Ghussal(غسل) he bathed himself, then he came back.

738
00:58:16,551 --> 00:58:17,685
Then she gave him the scrolls.

739
00:58:19,466 --> 00:58:24,209
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه started reciting the Ayaat(آيات) in the scroll.

740
00:58:25,513 --> 00:58:26,874
بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَنِ الرَّحِيمِ َ۞

741
00:58:27,652 --> 00:58:28,352
 طه۞

742
00:58:29,146 --> 00:58:32,286
مَا أَنْزَلْنَا عَلَيْكَ الْقُرْآنَ لِتَشْقَى۞

743
00:58:33,226 --> 00:58:35,277
إِلَّا تَذْكِرَةً لِمَنْ يَخْشَى۞

744
00:58:36,259 --> 00:58:40,025
تَنْزِيلًا مِمَّنْ خَلَقَ الْأَرْضَ وَالسَّمَاوَاتِ الْعُلَى۞

745
00:58:41,161 --> 00:58:43,093
الرَّحْمَنُ عَلَى الْعَرْشِ اسْتَوَى۞

746
00:58:43,981 --> 00:58:48,367
لَهُ مَا فِي السَّمَاوَاتِ وَمَا فِي الْأَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا وَمَا تَحْتَ الثَّرَى۞

747
00:58:49,284 --> 00:58:52,321
وَإِنْ تَجْهَرْ بِالْقَوْلِ فَإِنَّهُ يَعْلَمُ السِّرَّ وَأَخْفَى َ ۞

748
00:58:53,029 --> 00:58:56,490
اللَّهُ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا هُوَ لَهُ الْأَسْمَاءُ الْحُسْنَى َ۞

749
00:58:58,888 --> 00:59:00,504
Translation of the Ayaat(آيات)

750
00:59:01,564 --> 00:59:06,346
We have not sent down the Qur’an to you to be occasion for you for your distress,

751
00:59:07,529 --> 00:59:12,075
but only as an admonition to those, who fear Allah.

752
00:59:13,352 --> 00:59:17,156
A revelation from Him, Who created the earth and heavens on high.

753
00:59:17,660 --> 00:59:22,187
Allah the Most Gracious is firmly established on the throne.

754
00:59:23,253 --> 00:59:26,321
To Him belongs what's in the heavens and on earth

755
00:59:26,990 --> 00:59:29,874
and all between them and all beneath the soil.

756
00:59:30,808 --> 00:59:33,039
If you pronounce the words aloud

757
00:59:33,621 --> 00:59:40,085
it is no matter for verily He knows what is secret and what is yet more hidden.

758
00:59:40,606 --> 00:59:45,911
Allah there is no god be He to Him belongs the Most beautiful names.

759
00:59:47,576 --> 00:59:50,338
When Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) recited these Ayaat(آيات) he said:

760
00:59:50,897 --> 00:59:54,326
Is this what Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) was against?

761
00:59:57,310 --> 01:00:01,609
The One, Who has spoken these words needs to be worshipped.

762
01:00:02,871 --> 01:00:04,293
دُلُّوْنِي عَلَى محمد

763
01:00:04,318 --> 01:00:05,462
Where is Muhammad(محمد)?

764
01:00:07,303 --> 01:00:12,176
So, when they felt that he was honest and sincere in his desire to become a muslim.

765
01:00:12,567 --> 01:00:16,330
They told him, where Rasool Allah ﷺ was meeting the Sahabah(صحابه).

766
01:00:18,554 --> 01:00:22,092
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه walks down the streets of Makkah

767
01:00:22,117 --> 01:00:25,816
but this time with the completely different intension.

768
01:00:27,581 --> 01:00:31,658
He goes to Dar-Ul-Arqam(دارالارقم) and he knocks on the door.

769
01:00:33,941 --> 01:00:36,977
He was walking down the streets of Makkah

770
01:00:37,756 --> 01:00:41,378
and he goes to the Dar-Ul-Arqam(دارالارقم) and he knocks on the door.

771
01:00:42,970 --> 01:00:47,644
The Sahabah(صحابه) peek and see that it's Umar(عُمَر). So they all sit down.

772
01:00:50,434 --> 01:00:54,745
Hamza(حمزه) looks at them and says: What's wrong with you? They say, it's Umar(عُمَر)!

773
01:00:56,211 --> 01:00:59,161
What did Hamza(حمزه) say? He said: So what if it's Umar(عُمَر)!

774
01:01:00,266 --> 01:01:05,771
See, no one can say that but Hamza(حمزه), the rest were sitting.

775
01:01:06,588 --> 01:01:10,053
Nobody wanted to open the door. No one wanted to deal with Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمربن خطاب)

776
01:01:10,447 --> 01:01:12,576
But the Hamza(حمزه) is the one, who can handle that.

777
01:01:13,514 --> 01:01:15,521
He was the knight of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

778
01:01:16,148 --> 01:01:17,688
He said: So what if it's Umar(عُمَر)?

779
01:01:18,243 --> 01:01:20,894
If he came for good, then he is welcome,

780
01:01:21,202 --> 01:01:24,415
if he came for evil, then we will gonna kill him with his own sword.

781
01:01:26,310 --> 01:01:29,454
Because remember Umar(عُمَر) was hanging his sword on his neck.

782
01:01:32,574 --> 01:01:37,528
Hamza(حمزه) opens the door and they, he and another Sahabi(صحابي), they hold Umar(عمر) by his arms

783
01:01:38,443 --> 01:01:44,535
and they bring him to Rasool Allah ﷺ. Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Arsiloo(اَرْسِلُوُهْ), Leave him alone!

784
01:01:45,555 --> 01:01:49,044
So, Hamza(حمزه) and the other Sahabi(صحابي), they released Umar(عُمَر).

785
01:01:50,477 --> 01:01:53,303
Now, Rasool Allah ﷺ even though he was shorter than Umar(عُمَر),

786
01:01:54,676 --> 01:01:58,398
but when Rasool Allah ﷺ wants that strength he has strength of thirty men.

787
01:01:59,628 --> 01:02:05,305
Rasool Allah ﷺ grabs Umar(عُمَر) by his clothes and pulls him towards him and says,

788
01:02:05,873 --> 01:02:07,960
why did you come here son of Khattab(خطاب)?

789
01:02:08,501 --> 01:02:11,639
Aren’t you going to stop fighting Islam, until Allah destroys you.

790
01:02:13,050 --> 01:02:15,607
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: O Messenger of Allah,

791
01:02:15,939 --> 01:02:20,247
I have came here for no reason other than believing in Allaah and His Messenger.

792
01:02:21,228 --> 01:02:23,121
Rasool Allah ﷺ made Takbeer(تكبير).

793
01:02:23,557 --> 01:02:25,185
Now, none of the other Sahabah(صحابه) were there,

794
01:02:25,210 --> 01:02:27,346
they weren't seeing what was happening they were hiding.

795
01:02:28,603 --> 01:02:31,482
When they heard the Takbeer(تكبير) of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

796
01:02:31,551 --> 01:02:35,520
the whole place erupted in Takbeer(تكبير), they couldn't believe it.

797
01:02:36,176 --> 01:02:41,983
It just erupted in Takbeer(تكبير) and it was so loud, they had to immediately, disperse,

798
01:02:42,940 --> 01:02:44,454
because everybody else could hear it.

799
01:02:46,093 --> 01:02:49,272
That were their happiness, with the Islam of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب).

800
01:02:52,475 --> 01:02:58,501
Khabaab Ibn Arat(خباب ابن ارت) when Umar(عُمَر) was reading the scrolls,

801
01:02:58,597 --> 01:03:02,212
and he said: I want to go and meet Muhammadﷺ he came out of hiding

802
01:03:03,215 --> 01:03:09,228
and he said: O Umar(عُمَر) I think that Allah has accepted the Dua(دُعَا) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

803
01:03:09,832 --> 01:03:11,522
Rasool Allah ﷺ had made a Dua(دُعَا)

804
01:03:11,547 --> 01:03:18,071
اَلَّلهُمَّ اَعِزَّ الّاِسْلَامْ بِاَحَبِّ (عُمْرَيْنِ) الرَّجُلَيْنِ اِلَيْكْ عمرو بن هشام او عمر بن الخطاب

805
01:03:20,450 --> 01:03:26,986
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: O Allah honour Islam with one of the two men, the most beloved of the two men,

806
01:03:27,011 --> 01:03:30,574
بِاَحَبِّ الرَّجُلَيْنِ اِلَيْكْ عمرو بن هشام او عمر بن الخطاب

807
01:03:30,701 --> 01:03:32,543
Either Amr Bin Hisham(عمرو بن هشام) or Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب).

808
01:03:32,747 --> 01:03:35,554
Who is Amr Bin Hisham(عمرو بن هشام)? Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل)!

809
01:03:36,378 --> 01:03:40,213
Rasool Allah ﷺ made Du’a(دعا), and said: O Allah honour Islam with one of the two,

810
01:03:40,668 --> 01:03:44,053
the one whom you love most, Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) or Umar(عُمَر).

811
01:03:46,762 --> 01:03:49,727
Why did Rasool Allah ﷺ make a Dua(دُعَا) specific for these two men?

812
01:03:51,934 --> 01:03:58,955
Because there strength would turn into strength for Islam.

813
01:04:00,282 --> 01:04:05,546
Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) was a leader of his people, he was a very wise man.

814
01:04:05,586 --> 01:04:09,028
You know people have this impression of Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) as being a monster.

815
01:04:09,595 --> 01:04:12,714
No, Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) was a strong man,

816
01:04:13,523 --> 01:04:20,393
he was a straight forward person, he was committed to his objectives.

817
01:04:21,286 --> 01:04:27,864
He was a hard worker and he was very wise and intelligent.

818
01:04:28,955 --> 01:04:32,093
So, the people gave him a name and his real name is Amr Bin Hisham(عمرو بن هشام).

819
01:04:32,118 --> 01:04:35,931
His name is not Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل), his name is Amr Bin Hisham(عمرو بن هشام)

820
01:04:36,302 --> 01:04:42,395
but because of his wisdom, he was given the name Abul-Hakam(أبوالحكم), the father of wisdom.

821
01:04:44,706 --> 01:04:49,761
Now, Rasool Allah ﷺ gave him the name Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل), the father of Ignorance.

822
01:04:50,516 --> 01:04:54,767
Why? Because no matter how wise you are, no matter how intelligent you are,

823
01:04:55,075 --> 01:04:58,045
if your intelligence would not leads you towards Islam

824
01:04:58,070 --> 01:04:59,715
then you have no intelligence whatsoever.

825
01:05:00,412 --> 01:05:02,351
If your mind doesn’t take you to believe,

826
01:05:02,376 --> 01:05:04,428
لا اله الا الله و ان محمد رسول الله

827
01:05:04,682 --> 01:05:05,678
Then you don’t have mind.

828
01:05:07,121 --> 01:05:09,196
No, matter how intelligent people think you are,

829
01:05:09,576 --> 01:05:14,933
if you do not use your intellect take it towards Islam then you don’t have intellect whatsoever.

830
01:05:16,487 --> 01:05:19,081
And that would be admission of Kuffar(كفار) on the Day of Judgment.

831
01:05:19,106 --> 01:05:23,739
وَقَالُوا لَوْ كُنَّا نَسْمَعُ أَوْ نَعْقِلُ مَا كُنَّا فِي أَصْحَابِ السَّعِيرِ۞

832
01:05:24,262 --> 01:05:29,684
If we had any understanding or if our ears could hears, we would not be here,

833
01:05:30,326 --> 01:05:32,030
we have no understanding whatsoever.

834
01:05:32,987 --> 01:05:35,116
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ gave him the name Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل).

835
01:05:36,535 --> 01:05:40,907
Allahعَزّ وجَلّ accepted the Dua(دُعَا) of Rasool Allah ﷺ and chose Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

836
01:05:45,747 --> 01:05:52,804
There is another incident that happened with Umar(عمر) and it

837
01:05:53,541 --> 01:05:54,934
brought him closer to Islam.

838
01:05:56,844 --> 01:05:59,342
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) in his Jahiliyah(جاهليه) used to be a heavy drinker.

839
01:06:00,376 --> 01:06:01,596
He used to love his wine.

840
01:06:03,978 --> 01:06:08,110
And he had Nudama'a(نُدَ مَاء), Nudama'a(نُدَ مَاء) are your drinking partners.

841
01:06:10,984 --> 01:06:12,511
One night it was very late

842
01:06:13,757 --> 01:06:17,276
he went around to the pubs of Makkah all them were closed,

843
01:06:18,147 --> 01:06:20,649
first pub nobody was there, second pub nobody was there.

844
01:06:21,171 --> 01:06:24,622
He didn’t find any of his drinker partners, its too late.

845
01:06:27,948 --> 01:06:31,347
So he decided well, if there was nothing else to do, why not go and make Tawaf(طواف).

846
01:06:33,625 --> 01:06:36,031
So, he goes to Al-Ka’aba(اَلْكَعْبَه), there is nothing better to do.

847
01:06:36,151 --> 01:06:40,025
He goes to Al-Ka’aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) and who does he see there?

848
01:06:40,572 --> 01:06:44,152
This late hour at night nobody there, who does he see?

849
01:06:45,109 --> 01:06:51,528
Muhammadﷺ is praying. At this late hour when everybody is asleep.

850
01:06:51,917 --> 01:06:55,847
Rasool Allah ﷺ is standing in front of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) making Ruko'o(ركوع) and Sujood(سجود).

851
01:06:57,834 --> 01:07:02,472
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: Well why don't I strike fear

852
01:07:04,039 --> 01:07:06,896
in the heart of Muhammadﷺ, it's me and him alone.

853
01:07:08,486 --> 01:07:13,066
So, what he does, he goes behind Al-Ka’aba(اَلْكَعْبَه), so Rasool Ullah cannot see him.

854
01:07:14,272 --> 01:07:18,886
And he slides between Al-Ka’aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) and the Cloth of the Al-Ka’aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

855
01:07:18,911 --> 01:07:20,233
Al-Ka’aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) is covered in a cloth,

856
01:07:20,492 --> 01:07:22,963
so Umar(عُمَر) is standing in between Al-Ka’aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) and the cloth.

857
01:07:23,987 --> 01:07:26,428
And he begins to sneak around Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

858
01:07:27,412 --> 01:07:31,198
So, Rasool Ullah cannot see him, until he made it right in front of Rasool Ullah.

859
01:07:31,657 --> 01:07:34,880
But Rasool Ullah cannot see him because he is behind the cloth of Al-Ka’aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

860
01:07:37,099 --> 01:07:40,218
What Umar(عُمَر) wanted to do, is to ambush Rasool Allah ﷺ.

861
01:07:42,152 --> 01:07:46,579
But when he gets there he was in the hearing range of Ayaat(آيات) of Qur’an.

862
01:07:47,747 --> 01:07:50,872
Now, the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) used to intentionally plugged their ears.

863
01:07:50,897 --> 01:07:56,792
So, that they won't hear Qur’an. But now, Umar(عُمَر) is right there within range,

864
01:08:01,227 --> 01:08:06,093
Umar(عُمَر) is listening attentively to the Ayaat(آيات) of Qur’an.

865
01:08:07,816 --> 01:08:14,007
Umar(عُمَر) said to himself: These must be the words of a poet, wonderful words,

866
01:08:14,222 --> 01:08:15,629
they must be words of a poet.

867
01:08:17,367 --> 01:08:20,122
Rasool Allah ﷺ was reciting the Surat-Al-Haaqah(سورة الحاقة),

868
01:08:21,362 --> 01:08:26,213
and the exact next Ayah(آية) after this thought came to mind of Umar(عُمَر) was,

869
01:08:26,957 --> 01:08:29,714
وَمَا هُوَ بِقَوْلِ شَاعِرٍ ۚ قَلِيلًا مَا تُؤْمِنُونَ۞

870
01:08:30,033 --> 01:08:32,948
"These are not the words of a poet, little did you believe".

871
01:08:35,569 --> 01:08:38,154
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was shocked and he immediately said:

872
01:08:38,446 --> 01:08:41,711
These must be words of a Kaahin(كاهن), of a fortune teller

873
01:08:41,736 --> 01:08:44,740
- how did he know what was in my heart? The next Ayah(آية) was,

874
01:08:44,765 --> 01:08:47,008
وَلَا بِقَوْلِ كَاهِنٍ ۚ قَلِيلًا مَا تَذَكَّرُونَ۞

875
01:08:47,201 --> 01:08:50,663
These are not the words of a fortune teller little do you remember.

876
01:08:52,557 --> 01:08:54,907
Umar(عمر) just froze in his tracks,

877
01:08:57,929 --> 01:08:59,279
these must be words of Allah.

878
01:09:00,984 --> 01:09:06,761
So, Allah was preparing him, for the important role that he is going to play in the future.

879
